from common import save
H = [
("What is a healthy diet?","A healthy diet has plenty of vegetables, fruit, whole grains (brown rice, millets, whole wheat), pulses, nuts, and some milk, eggs, fish or lean meat. Limit sugar, salt, fried food and processed snacks, and drink enough water (about 2–3 litres a day for adults).",["healthy food","how to eat healthy","healthy eating","good diet"]),
("How much water should I drink a day?","Most adults need about 2–3 litres of water a day (8–10 glasses), more in hot weather or when exercising. Pale yellow urine is a good sign you're drinking enough.",["how much water to drink","daily water intake"]),
("How much sleep do I need?","Adults need about 7–9 hours of sleep a night; teenagers 8–10 hours; school children 9–12 hours. Keep a regular bedtime and avoid screens for an hour before sleep.",["how many hours of sleep","sleep needed","how much sleep does a student need"]),
("How much exercise do I need?","Adults should get at least 150 minutes of moderate activity a week (such as 30 minutes of brisk walking, 5 days a week) plus muscle-strengthening twice a week. Children need about 60 minutes of activity every day.",["how much exercise","exercise benefits","daily exercise"]),
("What is diabetes?","Diabetes is when blood sugar stays too high because the body doesn't make enough insulin (Type 1) or can't use it well (Type 2, the common one). Signs: thirst, frequent urination, tiredness. Healthy food, exercise, weight control and medicines help manage it. Normal fasting blood sugar is about 70–100 mg/dL.",["diabetes","sugar disease","type 2 diabetes","normal blood sugar level"]),
("What is high blood pressure?","High blood pressure (hypertension) is when blood pushes too hard on artery walls, 140/90 mmHg or more. It often has no symptoms but raises the risk of heart attack and stroke. Less salt, exercise, a healthy weight and medicines help.",["hypertension","high bp","blood pressure high"]),
("What are the signs of a heart attack?","Heart attack signs: chest pain or pressure, pain spreading to the arm, jaw or back, breathlessness, sweating, nausea. Call an ambulance (108 in India) immediately; chewing an aspirin can help if the person isn't allergic.",["heart attack symptoms","heart attack signs"]),
("What is first aid for a burn?","For a burn: cool it under cool (not ice-cold) running water for 20 minutes, remove rings or tight items, cover loosely with cling film or a clean cloth. Don't apply ice, butter or toothpaste. Get medical help for large, deep or face burns.",["burn first aid","what to do for burns"]),
("What is first aid for bleeding?","For bleeding: press firmly on the wound with a clean cloth, keep pressing, and raise the injured part if possible. Don't remove objects stuck in the wound. Get medical help if the bleeding doesn't stop.",["bleeding first aid","how to stop bleeding"]),
("What is CPR?","CPR (cardiopulmonary resuscitation) keeps blood flowing when someone's heart stops. Call 108, then push hard and fast in the centre of the chest: about 100–120 pushes a minute, 5–6 cm deep, until help arrives.",["cpr","how to do cpr"]),
("What is the emergency number in India?","India's emergency numbers: 112 (all emergencies), 108 (ambulance in most states), 100 (police), 101 (fire), 1098 (child helpline) and 181 (women's helpline).",["emergency number india","ambulance number","police number india","112 india"]),
("What is dengue?","Dengue is a viral fever spread by the Aedes mosquito, which bites in the daytime. Symptoms: high fever, severe body and joint pain, headache, rash; platelets can fall. Rest, fluids and paracetamol help (avoid aspirin and ibuprofen). Prevent it by stopping water collecting around the home.",["dengue fever","dengue symptoms"]),
("What is malaria?","Malaria is caused by the Plasmodium parasite, spread by the female Anopheles mosquito. Symptoms: fever with chills and sweating. It's treated with antimalarial medicines; mosquito nets and repellents prevent it.",["malaria","malaria symptoms"]),
("What is tuberculosis?","Tuberculosis (TB) is a bacterial infection, usually of the lungs, spread through the air by coughing. Signs: a cough for over 2 weeks, fever, weight loss. It is curable with 6 months of medicines, free in India under the national TB programme.",["tb","tuberculosis","tb symptoms"]),
("What is the common cold?","The common cold is a virus infection of the nose and throat. It gets better by itself in about a week; rest, fluids and steam help. Antibiotics don't work on colds because they're caused by viruses.",["common cold","cold and cough","how to cure cold"]),
("What is anaemia?","Anaemia means too little haemoglobin in the blood, often from lack of iron, causing tiredness and pale skin. Iron-rich foods: green leafy vegetables, dates, jaggery, pulses, meat and eggs, with vitamin C to help absorption.",["anemia","anaemia","iron deficiency","iron rich foods"]),
("What is BMI?","BMI (Body Mass Index) = weight in kg ÷ (height in m)². Under 18.5: underweight; 18.5–24.9: healthy; 25–29.9: overweight; 30 or more: obese. (For Asians, 23 or more is often treated as overweight.) Try: \"bmi of 60 kg and 170 cm\", or ask me to \"make a BMI calculator app\".",["body mass index","bmi range","healthy bmi"]),
("How can I reduce stress?","Ways to reduce stress: regular exercise, enough sleep, deep breathing (breathe in for 4 counts, hold 4, out for 6), breaking big tasks into small steps, talking to someone you trust, and time away from screens. If stress or sadness lasts, talk to a doctor or counsellor. In India, the Tele-MANAS helpline is 14416.",["reduce stress","stress relief","how to relax","exam stress","anxiety tips"]),
("How can I study better?","Study tips: short focused sessions (25 minutes, then a 5-minute break: the Pomodoro method), test yourself instead of re-reading, space out revision over days, teach the topic to someone, sleep well, and keep your phone away while studying.",["study tips","how to study","how to concentrate","exam tips","how to remember what i study"]),
("What are the benefits of yoga?","Yoga improves flexibility, strength, balance and breathing, and reduces stress. International Yoga Day is on 21 June. Common asanas: Surya Namaskar, Tadasana, Vrikshasana, Bhujangasana and Shavasana.",["yoga","benefits of yoga","international yoga day","surya namaskar"]),
("What are antibiotics?","Antibiotics are medicines that kill bacteria or stop them growing. They don't work on viruses (colds, flu). Take the full course as the doctor says; misuse causes antibiotic resistance. Penicillin, discovered by Alexander Fleming in 1928, was the first.",["antibiotics","antibiotic resistance"]),
("What are the benefits of walking?","Daily walking strengthens the heart and lungs, helps control weight, blood sugar and blood pressure, strengthens bones, and lifts mood. 30 minutes a day, or about 7,000–10,000 steps, is a good goal.",["walking benefits","benefits of walking daily"]),
("What is protein and why do we need it?","Protein builds and repairs muscles, skin and organs and makes enzymes and hormones. Good sources: dal, chickpeas, rajma, paneer, milk, curd, eggs, fish, chicken, soya and nuts. Adults need about 0.8–1 g per kg of body weight a day.",["protein foods","protein rich food","why do we need protein"]),
]
save("health", "Health and first aid", H)
